qx|A2|st||rh||ah|Board 2 IMPs   -   June 19, 2024|pn|hondo717,IraCT,danpsych,Sputniks|
md|4S54HJ4DKQT82CK985,SKJ2HQ9632DA43C42,SQ3HKT875D97CAQ76,SAT9876HADJ65CJT3|sv|n|MB|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Personally I would open 2@S. But with 2 Aces I understand if East passes because the hand has more defense than a normal preempt.|
PG| ***** 15 ***** |


mb|2S|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|lb|*bBid for West^^3S|mb|3S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|This is a very obvious 3@S bid. Whenever partner opens a weak-2 and you have 3 card support you must raise to 3, at least, unless you think you have game. The |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at|, says it is right to be in a 9 trick contract (3 level) with a 9 card fit, and is almost always correct.|

