%%%%%%Hand 3
https://tinyurl.com/285c6to4
qx|A3|st||rh||ah|Board 3 IMPs   -   June 19, 2024|pn|hondo717,danpsych,IraCT,Sputniks|
md|1SAJT94HJ84DKCQT98,SQ875HA2D432CAK62,SK3HK653DAT65C543,S62HQT97DQJ987CJ7|sv|e|MB|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I use the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule of 20^*N|CP||FP||at| to decide whether or not to open. In standard Rule of 20 you add HCP and the length of 2 longest suits. You open if the sum is 20 or more.|
PG| ***** 35 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|However, to count the hand's "Points" I use all |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=bergenstartingpoints,Bergen Starting Points^*N|CP||FP||at| rules except the ^*BLength^*n. So I add 1 for each ^*BQuality Suit^*n, subtract 1 for each ^*BDubious Shortness^*n, and add or subtract for excess ^*BAces/Tens^*n and for excess ^*BQueens/Jacks^*n [Adjust - 3]. I label this ^*BBergen Adjusted Points.^*n|
PG| ***** 36 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|My hand has 11 HCP, 1 Quality Suit point for the 3 honor suit in spades, 9 cards in the black suits, and less one point for singleton @DK for 20. Thus the hand is an opener.|
PG| ***** 37 ***** |


mb|1S|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|1N|mb|P|mb|2C|mb|P|mb|2S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I agree with 2@S bid. Some might bid 2N but that is a tad aggressive. This is a very typical forcing NT auction, where opener's rebid is a minor and responder corrects to the major with 2 card support.|
PG| ***** 38 ***** |


