%%%% Hand 4
https://tinyurl.com/26b8jg9j
qx|A4|st||rh||ah|Board 4 IMPs   -   June 19, 2024|pn|hondo717,danpsych,IraCT,Sputniks|
md|2SAK76HA52DT8C9863,SQ53H74DJ532CAJ75,S984HKQJT3DAKQ4CQ,SJT2H986D976CKT42|sv|b|
mb|P|mb|1H|mb|P|mb|1S|mb|P|mb|3D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I think 3@D is a very reasonable call. 2@D is somewhat of an underbid even discounting the @CQ. North has 15 HCP, 1 length point, and 2 quality suits for 18 |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=bergenstartingpoints,Bergen Starting Points^*N|CP||FP||at| enough for 3@D call.|
PG| ***** 58 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Bergen uses a rule that I don't agree with completely. He says if you have a 4 honor suit (which North does in hearts) you can pretend the suit is one longer than it is. If you use that rule, another possible bid for North would be 3@H.|
PG| ***** 59 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|MB|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now slam is possible with my hand although I am a tad light. With 3 |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=quicktricks,Quick Trick^*N|CP||FP||at| my hand is definitely in slam territory, though I do have a problem because although we are forced to game 3@H is simply a preference for hearts and does not show a limit raise. What I was expecting to happen was that North would rebid say 1N, or 2@C, or 2@D and I would jump to 3@H to show my 3 card limit raise (10-12 with 3 hearts).|
PG| ***** 60 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|But I can not do that on this auction. I could bid 4@H. I guess that would show a limit raise, but it takes up a lot of room.|
PG| ***** 61 ***** |


mb|3H|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|4C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Since we agreed on hearts 4@C is an interesting bid. I not sure what I would make that opposite a 3@H call. It must be a control bid.  |
PG| ***** 62 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|That said, because I have spades controlled, and North showed slam interest by control bidding clubs and bid diamonds I am assuming he is worried about spades but want to look for slam. So with my very good hand given the bidding I will bid RKCB.|
PG| ***** 63 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I play |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=kickback,Kickback^*N|CP||FP||at| RKCB meaning when hearts are trump 4@S is RKCB. The reason to play that is to make it possible to do the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=queenask,Queen Ask^*N|CP||FP||at| when the response is the 2nd step.|
PG| ***** 64 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|If you play 4N as RKCB when hearts are trump then if partner bids 5@D, the RKCB bidder can't ask for the Queen since 5@H is to play and 5@S goes past 5@H.|
PG| ***** 65 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|But if you play 4@S as RKCB then 5@C would be the response with 1 or 4, and 5@D can then be the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=queenask,Queen Ask^*N|CP||FP||at|.|
PG| ***** 66 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|As to why 4@C is correct. A control bid shows first or second round control. More often than not it is an Ace or King but it can be a singleton or void, as it is here. It is not the @CQ that is the control, it is the singleton.|
PG| ***** 67 ***** |


mb|P|mb|4S|an|rkcb|
PG| ***** 68 ***** |


mb|P|mb|5H|an|2 keys and the @HQ|
PG| ***** 69 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So partner has 2 keys and the @HQ and I have 2 key cards. Any time you bid RKCB you should bid slam if a) you have all 5 key cards or b) you have 4 key cards and the trump Queen. So since our side has 4 keys and the trump Queen, I should and will bid 6. Unfortunately we don"t have a particularly good fit, and slam is unlikely.|
PG| ***** 70 ***** |


mb|6H|mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 71 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|
pc|D9|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I don't like the @D9 lead but no undo is needed because it turns out not to make a difference. I prefer leading low from 3 small. Some people like to play "Top of Nothing" from 3 small and that is fine.|
PG| ***** 72 ***** |


