https://tinyurl.com/22flhqat
qx|A5|st||rh||ah|Board 5 IMPs   -   June 19, 2024|pn|hondo717,danpsych,Sputniks,IraCT|
md|3ST9HT52DT987CT952,SQ2HK84D643CK8763,SKJ4HAJ76DJ2CAQJ4,SA87653HQ93DAKQ5C|sv|n|
mb|1N?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Playing |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=dont,DONT^*N|CP||FP||at|, if your suit is spades, you have two ways of showing spades. One way is to just bid 2@S. The other way is to double which in |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=dont,DONT^*N|CP||FP||at| means a single suited hand. Partner then bids 2@C asking the doubler to pass with clubs or correct to their suit.|
PG| ***** 88 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|If you double and then bid 2@S that shows a stronger hand than bidding 2@S directly. In fact, if East had somewhat better spades I would recommend they double and then jump to 3@S. Playing DONT if you bid at the 3 level directly, that is a preempt. But if you double and jump to 3, that shows a really good hand.|
PG| ***** 89 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I don't think East is quite good enough to double and bid 3@S. But the hand certainly is good enough to double and bid 2@S.|
PG| ***** 90 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|
